# CHAPTER FIVE: MORNING ARRANGEMENTS
# 04:30 to 06:30. What Ari wants. Who helps. The room, the paper, six o'clock,
# a minute of the future, the fog, tomorrow, the Casio.

=== ch5_start
@chapter 5 "Morning Arrangements"
~ clk = 270
->> tick
@comp exchange
@set exchange
@cam inez_eye
@xwin 1 off
@xwin 2 lamp on "HOLD"
@xwin 3 wave 200 "DOOR 200"
@xwin 4 text x "209 DESK"
@view none
@amb exchange_relays
@clear
SOUND: A mug put down on a relay rack, which Inez would kill anybody else for doing.
INEZ: Right. What you can do. I'll say it once, plainly, and then it's yours.
INEZ: One. The room. The token's in your bag in G/1. Somebody fetches it. You go on 201. Somebody holds the place for twenty minutes. You come out of that basin hungry and cold and a person.
INEZ: Two. The paper. Either Sal's packet, which makes you the building's everything, or the old form, which just makes you you. That's separate from the room. You can do the room and pick either paper.
INEZ: Three. You stay on the line. I keep you on the frame, hold running on your {pref_hold}. But I'm sixty-eight and I sleep, so there'd be rules.
~ k_three_options = true
* [ask] "What rules?"
    -> ch5_rules
* [ask] "What would you do?"
    INEZ: Not my body. Not my call.
    INEZ: I'd want to know what it was like to be hungry, probably. That's me, though. I like knowing what things do.
    * [ask] "What rules? For staying on the line."
        -> ch5_rules
* [ask] "Can I change my mind later?"
    INEZ: The room's been here since fifty-one. It'll be here in a month. Sal's packet might not. The old form will. They printed a lot of them.
    INEZ: It's not now or never. It's now or later. Sal would say that's the same thing. It isn't.
    ~ k_reversible = true
    * [ask] "What rules? For staying on the line."
        -> ch5_rules

=== ch5_rules
INEZ: Calls between eight and eleven. Unless somebody's in trouble, and then any time, but they have to actually be in trouble.
INEZ: Nobody has to lend you their eyes. You ask, they can say no, and that's the end of it.
INEZ: You can say no as well. To calls. To anyone. Including me.
INEZ: I check the frame Mondays and Thursdays. I write down how, for whoever comes after me, because somebody will have to come after me.
INEZ: And nobody sits with you. You're not a vigil. You're a tenant.
~ k_shared_terms = true
* "What if the council finds the frame?"
    INEZ: Then we'll have a fight about it. They've forgotten it for twenty years. I'm counting on them being consistent.
    ~ k_shared_risk = true
* "A tenant."
    INEZ: Rent's the tape. You have to listen to whatever's on hold. That's the rent.
* "Okay."
-> ch5_jad_rings

=== ch5_jad_rings
~ clk = 280
->> tick
@ring jad
SOUND: Jad.
* [answer] Plug in.
    -> ch5_jad_call
* [decline] Let it ring.
    ~ jad_declined_ch5 = true
    SOUND: It rings itself out. He doesn't ring again.
    if jad_letter_ok:
        @text jad "Printing the letter. You said do it. I won't ring again unless you ring me. J."
    else:
        @text jad "I won't ring again unless you ring me. J."
    @callable jad ch5_jad_call_back
    -> ch5_hub

=== ch5_jad_call_back
~ jad_declined_ch5 = false
~ jad_rang_back = true
@acoustic shop
@call jad
@view none
JAD: You rang.
JAD: Thank you. I didn't think you would.
->> ch5_jad_body
@hangup
@callable jad off "At the shop."
return

=== ch5_jad_call
@acoustic shop
@call jad
@view none
@amb2 copyshop
->> ch5_jad_body
@hangup
@amb2 off
@callable jad off "At the shop."
-> ch5_hub

=== ch5_jad_body
~ answered_jad_ch5 = true
@set copyshop
@cam jad_eye
if jad_confess_mode == "kicked" or jad_confess_mode == "left":
    JAD: I'm at the shop. I'm going to say one thing and then you can hang up.
else:
    JAD: I'm at the shop.
JAD: Can I ask you something? You can say no. I'm asking.
if jad_letter_ok:
    JAD: You said do the letter. I've done it. It says it was me: my name, my form clinic, my one-page version. It separates you from their forms. Forty-two copies, one for under every door.
    JAD: I'm asking if you still want me to put them under the doors. Because once they're under the doors, they're under the doors.
else:
    JAD: Do you want me to print the letter? It says it was me. It takes you off their forms. Forty-two copies, one under every door.
    JAD: It costs about what the coach costs. That's not a reason. I'm just telling you what it costs.
~ jad_asked = true
* "Yes. Do it."
    ~ jad_letter_ok = true
    ~ jad_letter = "yes"
    JAD: Okay.
    JAD: Okay. Thank you for... okay.
* "No. Don't."
    ~ jad_letter = "no"
    ~ jad_letter_ok = false
    JAD: Right.
    A pause. The copier nearest him runs its light along the glass on its own.
    JAD: Right. Okay. I won't.
    ~ jad_accepted_no = true
    if jad_told_stop:
        JAD: You said don't do anything else for you. I asked anyway. I said I'd ask. I've asked.
* "Why are you asking me? It's your name on it."
    JAD: Because it's your name on everything else, and nobody asked you about any of that.
    * "Do it."
        ~ jad_letter_ok = true
        ~ jad_letter = "yes"
        JAD: Okay.
    * "Don't."
        ~ jad_letter = "no"
        ~ jad_letter_ok = false
        JAD: Okay. I won't.
        ~ jad_accepted_no = true
if jad_letter == "yes":
    ~ docs_letter = true
    @text_doc jad jad_letter "Here's what it says. Going under the doors now."
* [ask] {not holder_asked_jad} "Would you hold the place? If I go into the room."
    ~ holder_asked_jad = true
    JAD: Yes.
    JAD: I mean... yes, if you want me. Not because I owe you. I do owe you. That's not why.
    ~ holder_jad_ok = true
* "Where will you be at six?"
    JAD: Here. Then home. Then the coach is at ten past seven, if I'm getting it.
    JAD: I haven't decided. I keep not deciding. It's a skill.
    ~ k_harwick = true
* "Don't ring me again."
    ~ told_jad_away = true
    JAD: Okay.
    JAD: Okay. I won't.
    ~ jad_accepted_no = true
* "That's all?"
    JAD: That's all. I didn't want to do anything else without asking. I've been doing things without asking for about six weeks.
return

# ------------------------------------------------------------ the hub

=== ch5_hub
@comp exchange
@set exchange
@view none
~ tick_n = 0
->> tick
if clk >= 310 and not sal_nudged:
    ~ sal_nudged = true
    @text sal "Twenty minutes to half five. No pressure. Some pressure. S."
* [call][jack:kaye] {not ch5_kaye_done} Ring Mrs. Kaye. Her lamp's lit; she's up.
    ->> ch5_kaye
    -> ch5_hub
* [call][jack:teodor] {not ch5_teodor_done} Ring Teodor.
    ->> ch5_teodor
    -> ch5_hub
* [call][jack:nell] {not ch5_nell_done} Ring Nell.
    ->> ch5_nell
    -> ch5_hub
+ [ask] {not inez_ask_done} Ask Inez something.
    ->> ch5_inez_ask
    -> ch5_hub
* [call][jack:jad] {jad_declined_ch5 and not jad_rang_back} Ring Jad after all.
    ->> ch5_jad_call_back
    -> ch5_hub
+ [go] I know what I want.
    -> ch5_decide

# ------------------------------------------------------------ Mrs. Kaye

=== ch5_kaye
~ ch5_kaye_done = true
~ clk += 8
->> tick
@set building
@cam main
@acoustic flat
@call kaye
@view none
@amb2 kaye_kitchen
SOUND: A kettle coming to the boil, and a radio with the volume at one.
KAYE: Hello, dear. I thought it might be you. Nobody else rings at this time. Nobody else is awake at this time except that man on the fifth floor, and he only rings you.
* [ask] "Can I tell you what I am?"
    KAYE: Go on.
    * "I'm not from the council. I'm not a young woman with glasses. I'm not anyone yet."
        ~ told_kaye_truth = true
        KAYE: No. I gathered that, dear. I was there. I was sat on the cushion.
        KAYE: Still. It's nice to be told. People don't tell you things at my age, they tell your daughter.
    * "I'm what happened when you all rang the same number."
        ~ told_kaye_truth = true
        KAYE: Well. That's what I thought a council was, when I was a girl.
* "How are you?"
    KAYE: Tired. Wide awake. Seventy-nine. Is that three things or one?
if p_kaye_thursday == "made":
    KAYE: You said you'd come on Thursday. In your message.
    * "I'll still come, if I can walk to the bus."
        ~ kaye_confirmed = true
        KAYE: If you can walk to the bus. That's fair. That's the honest way of putting it.
        ~ p_kaye_thursday = "conditional"
    * "I can't promise Thursday. I'm going to make sure somebody else can."
        ~ p_kaye_thursday = "renegotiated"
        ~ kaye_renegotiated = true
        KAYE: Oh.
        KAYE: Well. Thank you for saying. Before Thursday. That's something.
        ~ need_kaye_arr = true
    * "Let's talk about Thursday later."
        ~ kaye_deferred_thursday = true
        KAYE: Later's fine, dear. Later's most of what I've got.
else:
    KAYE: I shall need someone on Thursday, you know. For my eye.
    * "I'll take you. If I can walk by then."
        ~ p_kaye_thursday = "conditional"
        KAYE: If you can walk. That's fair.
    * "I'll make sure someone takes you."
        ~ p_kaye_thursday = "arranging"
        ~ need_kaye_arr = true
        KAYE: That's all I wanted, really. Someone. I don't need it to be anyone.
    * "I can't do Thursday."
        ~ p_kaye_thursday = "declined"
        ~ need_kaye_arr = true
        KAYE: No. No, well. I'll ask the surgery about the hospital car.
        KAYE: They send a man. He smokes.
KAYE: I'd got used to the idea of you, you know. The glasses and so on.
KAYE: I'll get used to the other one.
@hangup
@amb2 off
return

# ------------------------------------------------------------ Teodor

=== ch5_teodor
~ ch5_teodor_done = true
~ clk += 9
->> tick
@set office
@cam teodor_eye
@acoustic flat
@call teodor
@view none
TEODOR: Ari.
TEODOR: I've been up. I'm always up. What do you need?
-> ch5_teodor_q

=== ch5_teodor_q
* [ask] "The coat. Do you want it back?"
    if told_teodor_not_him:
        TEODOR: Keep it.
        TEODOR: It's cold down there. He's not coming for it. And you're not him, so it's just a coat now. It's allowed to be just a coat.
        ~ coat_fate = "kept"
    else:
        TEODOR: I...
        TEODOR: Yes. I think yes. I'll hang it back up. Is that all right?
        * "It's yours. Of course."
            ~ coat_fate = "returned"
            TEODOR: Thank you.
        * "I'd like to keep it. If that's all right."
            ~ coat_fate = "kept"
            TEODOR: Then keep it. The sleeves are long.
            ARI: I know.
    -> ch5_teodor_q
* [ask] {need_kaye_arr or p_kaye_thursday == "made" or p_kaye_thursday == null} "Could you take Mrs. Kaye to St Anne's on Thursday?"
    TEODOR: St Anne's. Eye unit. Round by the car park, the lift that smells of soup.
    TEODOR: I know the way. I took my wife there, a long time ago. Yes.
    ~ arr_kaye_offer_teodor = true
    ~ arr_kaye = "teodor"
    -> ch5_teodor_q
* [ask] {not holder_asked_teodor} "Would you hold the place? In the room, for twenty minutes."
    ~ holder_asked_teodor = true
    if told_teodor_not_him or teodor_gentle:
        TEODOR: Yes.
        TEODOR: I held a line four years for somebody who never picked up. I can hold one twenty minutes for somebody who does.
        ~ holder_teodor_ok = true
    else:
        TEODOR: I'd want to.
        TEODOR: I don't think I should. I'd be holding it for the wrong person. You'd come out and I'd be looking for the length in the sleeves.
        ~ holder_teodor_declined = true
    -> ch5_teodor_q
* [ask] "If the desk's gone, who helps at three in the morning?"
    TEODOR: I'm up at three anyway. If somebody needs somebody at three, I can be somebody.
    TEODOR: Not every night. My knees. Most nights.
    ~ rota_teodor = true
    -> ch5_teodor_q
* "That's all. Thank you."
    TEODOR: It's nothing. It's three in the morning somewhere.
    @hangup
    return

# ------------------------------------------------------------ Nell

=== ch5_nell
~ ch5_nell_done = true
~ clk += 8
->> tick
@set nell
@cam nell_eye
@acoustic flat
@call nell
@view none
@amb2 flat_night
NELL: I'm up. Tobi's up. Nobody in this flat has slept since the moth.
if not b_nell_phone and not nell_apology:
    NELL: You read my phone.
    * "I did. I'm sorry."
        ~ nell_apology = true
        NELL: Okay. Right. Thank you. Don't again.
    * "It said Fake Ari."
        NELL: It did. It doesn't now. Moving on.
-> ch5_nell_q

=== ch5_nell_q
* [ask] {need_kaye_arr or p_kaye_thursday == "made" or p_kaye_thursday == null} "Could you take Mrs. Kaye on Thursday?"
    NELL: Thursday. What time?
    ARI: The 36 at five to eight.
    NELL: I've got Thursday off, as it happens. I'll take Bernadette. Don't tell her I swapped it.
    ARI: Did you swap it?
    NELL: I'm going to swap it.
    ~ arr_kaye_offer_nell = true
    ~ arr_kaye = "nell"
    -> ch5_nell_q
* [ask] "If the desk's gone, who does the things the desk did?"
    NELL: Us. Obviously. That's the joke, isn't it. It was always going to be us.
    NELL: I can do Tuesday nights. Not every Tuesday. Most. I'm doing a group chat. An actual one, with actual people in it. No offence.
    ~ rota_nell = true
    -> ch5_nell_q
* [ask] "What's Tobi doing up?"
    NELL: Doing your face. For the drawing. She wants to know what colour your eyes are.
    * "Tell her to pick."
        ~ pref_eyes = "tobi"
        NELL: She'll pick green. She picks green for everything. Even me.
    * "Grey. Like the tiles in the dark."
        ~ pref_eyes = "grey"
        NELL: Grey like the tiles in the dark. She'll love that. She'll ask what tiles.
    * "I don't know yet."
        ~ pref_eyes = "unknown"
        NELL: She says she'll leave them for later, then. She's very relaxed about leaving things for later. She gets that from me.
    -> ch5_nell_q
* "That's all. Go to sleep."
    NELL: Funny. You're funny. Night, Ari.
    @hangup
    @amb2 off
    return

# ------------------------------------------------------------ Inez

=== ch5_inez_ask
* [ask] {not holder_asked_inez} "Would you hold the place?"
    ~ holder_asked_inez = true
    if b_inez:
        INEZ: Yes. I've held worse. I held the second floor together with a Virgin for fifteen years.
    else:
        INEZ: Yes. I'll hold it properly. I won't be chatty.
        INEZ: I don't need to like you to do it right.
    ~ holder_inez_ok = true
    return
* [ask] "Would you check the frame for me? Mondays and Thursdays. If I stay."
    INEZ: I already said. It's already written down.
    ~ rota_inez = true
    return
* [ask] {not k_reversible} "Can I change my mind later?"
    INEZ: It's now or later. Not now or never.
    ~ k_reversible = true
    return
* [ask] {not k_shared_terms} "What would the rules be? For staying on the line."
    ->> ch5_rules_short
    return
* "Nothing. Never mind."
    ~ inez_ask_done = true
    INEZ: Mm.
    return

=== ch5_rules_short
INEZ: Calls eight till eleven, unless someone's actually in trouble. Nobody has to lend you their eyes. You can say no too. I check the frame Mondays and Thursdays, and I write down how. Nobody sits with you. You're a tenant, not a vigil.
~ k_shared_terms = true
return

# ------------------------------------------------------------ the decision

=== ch5_decide
~ rota_count = 0
if rota_nell:
    ~ rota_count += 1
if rota_teodor:
    ~ rota_count += 1
if rota_inez:
    ~ rota_count += 1
if jad_letter_ok:
    ~ rota_count += 1
INEZ: Go on, then.
* "I want to come through. And take the job."
    ~ end_body = true
    ~ end_appointment = "accepted"
    INEZ: The room and the packet. Right.
    -> ch5_holder
* "I want to come through. Not the job."
    ~ end_body = true
    ~ end_appointment = "refused"
    INEZ: The room and the old form. Right.
    -> ch5_holder
* {k_shared_terms} "I want to stay on the line. For now."
    ~ end_body = false
    ~ end_appointment = "none"
    INEZ: On the frame, then. Under the rules.
    INEZ: Say yes to the rules. Out loud. I want it said.
    * "Yes. To the rules."
        ~ shared_consent = true
        INEZ: Good.
    * "Yes. And I want to be able to change my mind."
        ~ shared_consent = true
        ~ k_reversible = true
        INEZ: That's the first rule. I just didn't say it.
    -> ch5_shared
* {not k_shared_terms} "Tell me about staying on the line first."
    ->> ch5_rules_short
    -> ch5_decide
+ "Not yet. I want to talk to someone first."
    -> ch5_hub

=== ch5_holder
if holder_jad_ok or holder_teodor_ok or holder_inez_ok:
    INEZ: Who's holding the place?
else:
    INEZ: Somebody has to hold the place. Who are you asking?
* {holder_jad_ok} "Jad said he would."
    ~ holder = "jad"
* {not holder_asked_jad and not told_jad_away} Ask Jad.
    ~ holder_asked_jad = true
    ~ asked_jad_now = true
    @sent jad "Would you hold the place? In the room. Twenty minutes."
    @text jad "Yes. On my way. Five minutes."
    ~ holder_jad_ok = true
    ~ holder = "jad"
* {holder_teodor_ok} "Teodor said he would."
    ~ holder = "teodor"
* {not holder_asked_teodor and (told_teodor_not_him or teodor_gentle)} Ask Teodor.
    ~ holder_asked_teodor = true
    TEODOR: Yes. Of course yes. I'm coming down.
    ~ holder_teodor_ok = true
    ~ holder = "teodor"
* {holder_inez_ok} "You. If you still will."
    ~ holder = "inez"
    INEZ: I said I would.
* {not holder_asked_inez} "You. Would you?"
    ~ holder_asked_inez = true
    ~ holder_inez_ok = true
    ~ holder = "inez"
    if b_inez:
        INEZ: Yes.
    else:
        INEZ: Yes. Properly. Not chatty.
INEZ: And somebody fetch the token out of that bag.
if holder == "jad":
    JAD: I'm getting it. I've got it. It's in my hand.
elif holder == "teodor":
    TEODOR: I'm in the office. I have it. It's heavier than I thought.
else:
    INEZ: I'll get it myself. Nobody touch my frame while I'm gone. You especially.
if not coat_fate:
    INEZ: And bring the coat. It's cold in there.
elif coat_fate == "kept":
    INEZ: And bring the coat. It's yours now, Teodor says. It's cold in there.
else:
    INEZ: Take my coat, then. It's cold in there. It'll be short in the arms. Everything's short in the arms on somebody.
-> ch5_arrival

# ------------------------------------------------------------ the arrival

=== ch5_arrival
~ clk = 305
->> tick
@comp room
@set receiving
@cam main
@view plan
@acoustic tiles
@amb receiving_room
@clear
The room, by its shape: cold tiles, the basin, the drain. The handset on 201 has somebody at it. You can feel the line go warm the way a hand warms a bannister.
SOUND: A brass token dropping into a meter. A crank, turned three times. Water, starting somewhere far off and coming nearer in the pipes.
@state meter on
@state cradle on
~ arrival_started = true
if holder == "jad":
    ->> hold_jad
elif holder == "teodor":
    ->> hold_teodor
else:
    ->> hold_inez
-> ch5_rupture

=== hold_jad
JAD: Okay. I'm on. I'm holding. Is that how you say it? I'm holding the place.
JAD: Inez says I have to keep talking. I can do that. I can do that all day. People pay me not to.
* "Tell me about paper."
    JAD: Paper. Right. Eighty gsm is normal. Hundred is posh. A hundred and twenty is someone's wedding. Three hundred's a card, and anything over that you shouldn't put through my machine, and people do.
* "Tell me about the dog."
    JAD: The lurcher. Eleven. The ninth photo. She came back at close, you know. After. To buy a frame. We don't sell frames. I sold her a frame.
* "Tell me something true."
    JAD: I'm scared I'll say the wrong thing and you'll come out wrong.
    JAD: That's not how it works. Inez says that's not how it works. I'm scared anyway.
@state fog on
SOUND: The water's in the basin now. The tiles above it have fogged in a patch the length of a person.
JAD: Still here?
ARI: Still here.
JAD: Good.
JAD: I never asked you what you wanted. All night. I asked you where you were and what you remembered. I didn't ask what you wanted.
if end_appointment == "accepted":
    JAD: You're doing the job. Okay. You can stop, you know. You can quit it. You can quit it and still live here. I'll still ring.
    ~ jad_right_to_stop = true
elif end_appointment == "refused":
    JAD: You're not doing the job. Good. I mean, not good. Yours. Good that it's yours.
JAD: Five more minutes, Inez says. Five more minutes of me talking about paper.
return

=== hold_teodor
TEODOR: I'm here. I'm holding.
TEODOR: Inez says talk. I'm not a talker. I was a tram mechanic. We talked to trams.
* "Talk to me like a tram."
    TEODOR: Good morning. You're making a noise in the front bogie. Nobody's ever made that noise. I'll have to take you apart and I'll put you back together better.
    TEODOR: That's what we said. Mostly we said worse things.
* "Tell me about your lengths."
    TEODOR: Twenty. Deep end to shallow is twenty-five metres, so it's a kilometre if you count there and back as two, which I do. Then the chair. Then a hundred.
* "Tell me about Mikael."
    TEODOR: No.
    TEODOR: Later. Not while I'm holding this. I'd hold the wrong thing.
@state fog on
SOUND: The water in the basin. The fog on the tiles, the length of a person.
TEODOR: Still there?
ARI: Still here.
TEODOR: Good. Good.
TEODOR: I used to ring at three because nobody was awake to be bothered. You were awake. I'm sorry I bothered you.
* "You didn't."
* "You did. I didn't mind."
    TEODOR: That's the nicest thing anybody's said to me in four years, and it's a complaint.
TEODOR: Five more minutes. I'll count. I'm good at counting.
return

=== hold_inez
if b_inez:
    INEZ: I'm on. I'm holding. Talk to me or I'll talk to you, and I'll talk about relays.
else:
    INEZ: I'm on. I'm holding.
    INEZ: I said I wouldn't be chatty. I'll be a bit chatty. It's the rule.
* "Talk about relays."
    INEZ: Strowger. Nineteen fifties. A step-by-step selector goes up, then goes round. That's all it does. It goes up, and then it goes round, and it finds you.
    INEZ: It's the most beautiful thing I've ever looked after. Don't tell Celeste.
* "Tell me about Mr. Pardoe."
    INEZ: He counted to ten with his hand on your head. That's all I remember. That and the lights.
    INEZ: You've got that now as well, so I suppose that's two of us remembering it.
* "Tell me about Celeste."
    INEZ: She sings in the car. Badly. She rings on Sundays at nine and I let it ring twice so she knows I'm not waiting by it.
@state fog on
SOUND: The water in the basin. The fog on the tiles, the length of a person.
INEZ: Still there?
ARI: Still here.
INEZ: Good. That's what the handset's for. Somebody asks, somebody answers.
INEZ: Five more minutes.
return

=== ch5_rupture
@state cradle full
Weight, first. Like before.
And then it doesn't go.
@rupture
@comp call
@set receiving
@cam ari_eye
@view ari
@amb receiving_room
@music off
~ arrived = true
Tiles. A ceiling of small white tiles, low and close, the grout lines not quite straight.
That's how it looks. That's how it looks to you. Nobody is lending you anything.
Cold, everywhere the water isn't. Warm, everywhere it is. A weight on your chest that turns out to be your chest.
if holder == "jad":
    Someone at the edge of what you can see, with a phone receiver still at his ear, not saying anything, because he's forgotten how to stop holding.
elif holder == "teodor":
    Someone at the edge of what you can see, tall, holding a receiver in both hands, counting under his breath past a hundred.
else:
    Someone at the edge of what you can see, in overalls, with a receiver on her shoulder, looking at you the way she looks at a repair that's held.
